e": "1 tablespoon lime zest, plus 1/4 cup lime juice", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1/3 cup salsa verde", "quantity": ""}], "instructions": ["1. Preheat the oven to 450° F. 2. On a baking sheet, toss the fish pieces with olive oil, honey, Tajin, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, and a pinch of salt. Arrange in a single layer. Roast 10-15 minutes or until the fish is cooked to your liking. During the last minute, switch the oven to broil and broil until lightly charred. Set the fish aside.3. To make the jalapeño cream. Combine all ingredients in a bowl. Season with salt. 4. To make the salsa. Combine all ingredients in a bowl. 5. Spread the cream cheese on the bottom of your shells. Layer in the lettuce, fish, and salsa."], "meal_type": "Lunch / Dinner", "name": "Crispy BBQ Salmon Tacos with Avocado Mango Salsa and Jalapeño Cream", "nutrition": {"calcium_mg": "80", "calories": "684", "carbs_g": "30", "cholesterol_mg": "60", "fat_g": "18", "fiber_g": "4", "iron_mg": "1.5", "potassium_mg": "800", "protein_g": "22", "saturated_fat_g": "5", "sodium_mg": "600", "sugar_g": "6", "vitamin_a_mcg": "200", "vitamin_c_mg": "30", "vitamin_d_mcg": "10"}, "prep_time": "25 mins", "servings": "6", "total_time": "35 mins"}, "source": {"image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/meal-plan-chef.firebasestorage.app/o/recipe-extract-img%2Fac2d1c8ad6a04767a5e3fdd6c13a18b5.jpg?alt=media", "provider": "www.halfbakedharvest.com", "source_type": "Manual", "title": "Crispy BBQ Salmon Tacos with Avocado Mango Salsa and Jalapeño Cream", "type": "webpage", "url": "https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/crispy-bbq-salmon-tacos/"}, "tags": ["High Protein", "Easy"], "transcript": null}}
{"url": "https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/brown-butter-scallops/", "status": "success", "summary": {"http": 200, "seconds": 7.9, "name": "Brown Butter Scallops with Corn, Bacon, and Avocado Salad", "n_ingredients": 13, "n_steps": 1, "method": "jsonld", "cached": false, "sample_ingredients": ["4  strips bacon, chopped", "4 ears corn, kernels removed", "1/2 cup fresh basil, chopped"], "sample_steps": ["1.&nbsp;Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat.&nbsp;Add the bacon and cook until crisp. Remove the bacon from the s"]}, "full_response": {"extraction": {"confidence": 0.7, "method": "jsonld"}, "recipe": {"cook_time": "15 mins", "cuisine": "American", "description": "high fiber low carb keto gluten free balanced Brown Butter Scallops with Corn, Bacon, and Avocado S.", "diet_flags": ["High Fiber", "Low Carb", "Keto", "Gluten Free", "Balanced"], "ingredients": [{"name": "4  strips bacon, chopped", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "4 ears corn, kernels removed", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1/2 cup fresh basil, chopped", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "juice from 1 lemon", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "kosher salt and pepper", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1 pound large scallops", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "4 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "4 cloves garlic, smashed", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh thyme", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1 pinch crushed red pepper flakes", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "4 tablespoons butter", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1/4 cup dry white wine, such as Pinot Grigio or Sauvignon Blanc", "quantity": ""}, {"name": "1  avocado, sliced", "quantity": ""}], "instructions": ["1.&nbsp;Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat.&nbsp;Add the bacon and cook until crisp. Remove the bacon from the skillet and drain onto paper towels. Strain off all but 1 tablespoon of bacon grease from the skillet and return the skillet to medium-high heat. Add the corn and cook 3-4 minutes, until golden. Add 1 tablespoon butter and allow it to brown, about 3-5 minutes more. Remove the skillet from the heat and stir in basil, lemon juice, and a pinch each of salt and pepper. Spoon the corn out of the skillet and onto a platter.2. Wipe the skillet clean and return to medium high heat. Add the olive oil.&nbsp;When the oil shimmers, add the scallops and sear on both sides until browned, about 2-3 minutes. Add the remaining 2 tablespoons butter, the garlic, thyme,&nbsp;and crushed red pepper flakes. Cook until fragrant and the butter golden, about 3-4 minutes. Slowly pour in the wine, simmer 5 minutes. Remove from the heat.&nbsp;3. Spoon the scallops&nbsp;and any sauce left in the pan over the corn. Sprinkle&nbsp;the bacon over top. Finish with avocado and fresh herbs. Eat!&nbsp;"], "meal_type": "Lunch / Dinner", "name": "Brown Butter Scallops with Corn, Bacon, and Avocado Salad", "nutrition": {"calcium_mg": "50", "calories": "800", "carbs_g": "10", "cholesterol_mg": "71", "fat_g": "42", "fiber_g": "3", "iron_mg": "2", "potassium_mg": "600", "protein_g": "18", "saturated_fat_g": "13", "sodium_mg": "703", "sugar_g": "3", "vitamin_a_mcg": "300", "vitamin_c_mg": "10", "vitamin_d_mcg": "0"}, "prep_time": "10 mins", "servings": "4 servings", "total_time": "25 mins"}, "source": {"image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/meal-plan-chef.firebasestorage.app/o/recipe-extract-img%2F2173ba81c92343cca489d5b0af7b6c8e.jpg?alt=media", "provider": "www.halfbakedharvest.com", "source_type": "Manual", "title": "Brown Butter Scallops with Corn, Bacon, and Avocado Salad", "type": "webpage", "url": "https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/brown-butter-scallops/"}, "tags": ["Quick", "Easy"], "transcript": null}}
