o medium-high heat. 2. In a bowl, toss the chicken, seasoned salt, and chili powder together. Add 1/3 cup buffalo sauce. Grill the chicken until lightly charred, 5-8 minutes per side, depending on the size of your chicken. 3. Shred the meat and toss with 1/3 cup buffalo sauce. Reserve the remaining sauce for serving. Stuff a handful of cheese and chicken into each taco shell. Place the shells upright on the grill so nothing falls out. Cover and grill over low heat for 3-5 minutes until the cheese is melty. 4. Meanwhile, make the Jalapeño Ranch. Combine all ingredients in a jar, mixing until creamy. Then, season with salt.5. Toss the lettuce with ranch, cilantro, scallions, and lime juice. Top each taco with greens, avocado, and extra sauce. Yum!"], "meal_type": "Lunch / Dinner", "name": "Grilled Buffalo Ranch Chicken Tacos", "nutrition": {"calcium_mg": "250", "calories": "582", "carbs_g": "35", "cholesterol_mg": "90", "fat_g": "25", "fiber_g": "3", "iron_mg": "2", "potassium_mg": "800", "protein_g": "30", "saturated_fat_g": "6", "sodium_mg": "1200", "sugar_g": "2", "vitamin_a_mcg": "500", "vitamin_c_mg": "15", "vitamin_d_mcg": "0"}, "prep_time": "20 mins", "servings": "6", "total_time": "40 mins"}, "source": {"image": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/meal-plan-chef.firebasestorage.app/o/recipe-extract-img%2F929b350dee544ab6a914ae3cbcef6e59.jpg?alt=media", "provider": "www.halfbakedharvest.com", "source_type": "Manual", "title": "Grilled Buffalo Ranch Chicken Tacos", "type": "webpage", "url": "https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/grilled-buffalo-ranch-chicken-tacos/"}, "tags": ["High Protein", "Easy"], "transcript": null}}
